    "body": "Hmmm looks like there really isnt an elegant way to deal with this.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think about computing the `bitstring_energy` through a class method of the Result class rather than in the init function. \r\n\r\nIn the workflow, you can pass the hamiltonian class directly into that class method to compute the `bitstring_energy` if it is requested.\r\n\r\nIn the factory method, the user would have to manually do it himself.\r\n\r\nAlthough I guess, if we want the Result Object to just provide this information from the moment the Result Object is created in `OptimizeVQA`, then this current implementation works for that purpose.",
